SANDCASTLE PERF PROFILING — CONCLUSIVE BOTTLENECK FOUND (2026-05-31). Built a live perf harness (src/lib/perf.ts -> window.__sc.perf.snapshot(): per-stage timing rings for displayPixels/blit/exec/stdout/total/fps; getPerf() attaches lazily) and instrumented GuiDesktopApp.tick + XWindowCanvas.tick. WITNESSED live (localhost:3007 GUI desktop, browser session): per-frame stageMean exec=884ms vs displayPixels=1.08ms blit=2.76ms stdout=0.33ms parse=0.04ms — EXEC dominates ~300x; all the micro-opts (gen-gate, LUT, dirty-rect) are noise vs the VM exec. BUT the headline finding: the GUI render-once pump FREEZES at frame 1 in-browser. Root-caused via live pump-state mirror (__sc.gui.pump): re-tick path is correct (requestTicks=2, ticks=2 fire) but the 2nd runExclusive never resolves (inFlight stuck true; bare 2nd /xappdemo run with NO pushInput times out at 8s). CAUSE: webix blink-core.js:331 runElf calls Module._blinkenlib_run() — the MAIN-THREAD single-shot path — and its setupProgram/TearDown+InitBus RE-INIT ABORTS on the 2nd run (stated in the runConcurrent comment blink-core.js:370-372). So _blinkenlib_run is NOT re-entrant in-browser: every render-once app + every sequential runCommand freezes after the first exec. (Node works — libuv schedules differently.) FIX (webix, reachable, needs wasm rebuild): route runElf through the PROVEN re-entrant thread-slot path — vm_spawn(0) -> run_thread_slot(H,slot) -> poll thread_done_slot(slot) with _emscripten_main_thread_process_queued_calls pump -> thread_status_slot(slot); launchXClient (blink-core.js:442) already proves sequential slot reuse works in-browser. Also fixed in sandcastle GuiDesktopApp parse (was a SECONDARY bug): stdout carries a '$ xappdemo' shell-prompt prefix + trailing-space damage token -> take last line containing '|', default damage=1 on empty/NaN. SECONDARY perf notices (PRD rows): displayPixels walks 1.9MB every idle rAF (gate gen BEFORE copy); RGB565->RGBA per-pixel JS loop (LUT); setInterval(flush,15000) leaked in client-sandbox-store (never cleared); dead xpra path still imported in WindowRenderer.tsx. The worker-scheduling-vm-offthread row IS the same fix as the runElf-reentrancy fix, generalized.